{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumJRWoY3WbzH9ASpMZM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, the 3 MB / 10 MB compressed limits are gone. According to a Cloudflare changelog entry dated 2026-09-04, Workers on both the Free and Paid plans can now be up to **64 MiB uncompressed**, and there's no separate compressed limit anymore. Only the uncompressed bundle size counts, and you can check it with `wrangler deploy --outdir bundled/ --dry-run`.\n\nSome other Cloudflare pages, like the Workflows and Agents limits pages, still list the old 3 MB / 10 MB figures. They look outdated, so go by the main Workers limits page and the changelog. I'm going on the search results' summary of those two pages and didn't open them myself.\n\nSources:\n- [Limits · Cloudflare Workers docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/)\n- [Deploy larger Workers — up to 64 MiB for both free and paid plans · Changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-09-04-increased-worker-size-limit/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_read_input_tokens":24543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7df62f22-cef2-4628-a18c-c85cd8d96bd4","uuid":"3c36e284-6144-4ca0-8101-2bcedcfa8c68","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:47:21.498Z","request_id":"req_011CfumJRHRS72msenRJWhwN"}
